# Compose Performance (Telegram-level)

## Compose Stability

All model classes passed to composables MUST be stable to avoid unnecessary recomposition:

```kotlin
@Immutable
data class Success(val messages: List<DirectMessage>)
```

## LazyColumn rules

- Always provide `key` with a stable unique ID (Long preferred)
- Always provide `contentType` to enable item reuse across types
- Use index-based `items(count)` to avoid list allocation (no `asReversed()`)

```kotlin
items(
    count = messages.size,
    key = { messages[messages.size - 1 - it].id },
    contentType = { if (messages[messages.size - 1 - it].isMe) 0 else 1 }
) { index ->
    MessageBubble(messages[messages.size - 1 - index])
}
```

## Avoid allocation in composition

```kotlin
// BAD — new RoundedCornerShape every recomposition
Modifier.clip(RoundedCornerShape(16.dp))

// GOOD — hoist as top-level val
private val BubbleShapeSent = RoundedCornerShape(16.dp, 16.dp, 4.dp, 16.dp)
private val BubbleShapeReceived = RoundedCornerShape(16.dp, 16.dp, 16.dp, 4.dp)
```

Same for `Color`, `TextStyle`, `Modifier` chains — pre-compute and reuse.

## Regex and parsing

NEVER create Regex inside composable:

```kotlin
// BAD — Regex compiled every call
private fun parse(content: String): String {
    val match = Regex("pattern").find(content)
}

// GOOD — use shared util from ContentParser.kt (compiled once)
val content = remember(msg.content) { parseContentText(msg.content) }
```

## remember for formatting in list items

Always wrap computed values in `remember` inside list items:

```kotlin
val timeText = remember(dm.lastMessageTimestamp) { formatRelativeTime(dm.lastMessageTimestamp) }
```

## derivedStateOf for computed UI state

```kotlin
val showJumpToBottom by remember {
    derivedStateOf { listState.firstVisibleItemIndex > 5 }
}
```

Use `derivedStateOf` for any value computed from snapshot state that changes more often than the derived value.
